# Milestone: M3
# Covers: two strands enqueued FIFO; after a soft yield the first strand
#         goes to the tail and the second strand runs next (FIFO ordering
#         across yield boundaries — row 12 §3.4 single-entry make_runnable
#         invariant).
#
# blocked: cross-strand FIFO ordering across a yield boundary is a scheduler
#          internal, verified by C unit tests, not a chk target.  Distinguishing
#          a-then-b from b-then-a from a golden-diff fixture would require
#          freezing test-only host-observation hooks (an enqueue-without-drive
#          primitive plus a per-strand yield-boundary emitter) into the v1.0
#          embedding API — rejected on API-minimalism grounds; the final
#          quiescent state is order-independent.  FIFO scheduling order IS
#          covered in C, by
#          tests/rt/test_sched.c::yield_round_robins_in_fifo_order, which
#          detaches three strands that each append their own letter twice
#          across a yield and asserts the interleaving is ABCABC; the fork
#          half is separators_run_both_arms and join_waits_for_the_child
#          in the same file.
# matrix-row: scheduler-fifo
